he important error in your screenshot is:

Plain Text
postgresql@14-main.service: Can't open PID file
/run/postgresql/14-main.pid (yet?): Operation not permitted

This usually means the /run/postgresql directory has wrong permissions or is missing.

Run these commands one by one:

Step 1: Check PostgreSQL directory
Shell
ls -ld /run/postgresql
Step 2: Fix ownership
Shell
sudo chown postgres:postgres /run/postgresql
sudo chmod 775 /run/postgresql
Step 3: Check PostgreSQL configuration
Shell
sudo -u postgres /usr/lib/postgresql/14/bin/postgres -D /var/lib/postgresql/14/main -c config_file=/etc/postgresql/14/main/postgresql.conf

This command usually shows the exact error preventing PostgreSQL from starting.

Step 4: Check the log
Shell
tail -100 /var/log/postgresql/postgresql-14-main.log
Step 5: Verify data directory ownership
Shell
sudo chown -R postgres:postgres /var/lib/postgresql
 
Step 6: Try starting again
Shell
sudo pg_ctlcluster 14 main start
Step 7: Check status
Shell
pg_lsclusters

Expected:

Plain Text
14 main 5432 online postgres
 
